# RHOPALIAL EDGE — INNER

Project architecture from the user's Cnidaria source:
- four peer edge nodes when defined by source (e.g. TINH/KHÍ/THẦN/NHÂN);
- multiple local eye/sensor channels per edge;
- ULE/global channel → SPACE_STONE global landmark/reference;
- LLE/local channel → near-field obstacle/looming/local-motion relation;
- statolith/gravity relation → orientation frame only when real telemetry exists, otherwise project mapping;
- raw input → derived low-pass/salience view while raw pointer remains lineage;
- local RNS/interneuron → pacemaker threshold/phase modulation;
- first threshold → peer phase reset/sync → asymmetric action vector → motor/action → consequence → readback → next cycle.

Do not invent an unspecified sixth label in the user-declared six-eye/channel mapping.
Do not claim biological embodiment or hidden continuous sensing without actual source/provider telemetry.


